:: work {"position":"700,250"}
<<scenery dump>>
<<addHours 8>>\
<<set $player.workedToday = true>>\
You spend 8 hours working on your job as $player.job.name
<<cash $player.job.pay>>
You currently own ¤<<- $player.cash.toFixed(2)>>

<<keyOption [[Return home|home]] 🏠>>
<<if $slaves.length gt 1 >>
    <<set
        _hungryBasementSlaveCount = Basement.getHungrySlaves().length;
        _neededPizzas = Math.ceil((_hungryBasementSlaveCount * 3) / 8);
        _pizzasPrice = _neededPizzas * 9;
    >>\
    <<if _hungryBasementSlaveCount && !Player.has("pizza", _neededPizzas) && $player.cash gte _pizzasPrice>>\
        <<keyAction "Go buy pizza for all the hungry slaves in the basement (¤_pizzasPrice) and return home" 🍕>>\
            <<run
                $player.cash -= _pizzasPrice;
                Player.getInventory().add({
                    name:'Pizza',
                    description:'Median basic pizza',
                    count:_neededPizzas,
                    tags: ["player", "food", "consumable"]
                })
            >>
            <<addMinutes 10>>
            <<goto home>>
        <</keyAction>>: 10min detour\
    <</if>>\
<</if>>\
:: home {"position":"700,375"}
<<scenery home>>
You are currently in front of your home.
<<unlessEmergency>>
    <<keyOption [[Go inside|main]] 🚪>>
    <<include workOption>>\
    <<keyOption [[Go to the park|playground]] ⚽>>
    <<keyOption [[Go to the school|shool]] 🏫>>
    <<keyOption [[Head Into Town|centralPlaza]] ⛲>>
<</unlessEmergency>>\
:: centralPlaza

You head down the road a little ways, and think you can see the Towns Plaza dead ahead. <<addMinutes 7>> 
It takes you about 7 minutes to reach the Plaza and once you arrive you are rather surprised to see that the Plaza
isn't bustling as much as you thought it would be... Everyone must be in the other parts of town. You
look around for a map of some sort. But the closest thing you can find is a Signpost that says
Welcome to Honeycross, please enjoy your stay! It is clearly meant for tourists not the locals.
Underneath the welcome sign there are four arrows one pointing towards each District Of Honeycross.


Where would you like to go?

<<keyOption [[North|businessDistrict]] 🏬>>
<<keyOption [[Northwest|waterfrontDistrict]] 🚉>>
<<keyOption [[West|entertainmentDistrict]] 🧑‍🎤>>
<<keyOption [[East|residentialDistrict]] 🏠>>
<<keyOption [[South, Head Back Home|home]] 🏠>>


:: businessDistrict

You decide to head north into the Business District, It takes you about 5 minutes but you get there
<<addMinutes 5>> as you enter, the first thing you notice right off the bat is that the entire area 
lives up to it's name as it appears to be nothing but a Giant Labyrinth of Brick, Stone, and Concrete 
buildings ominously looming over you. You swear you can hear the screams of human torment and boredom
emanating all around you. This is as close to hell as you think you can get. You look around and notice
a building that looks so out of place here. It's called the Hard N' Ready lumber store. You are
both curious and intrigued... Maybe it's the name of the Building itself or how different it is from the 
rest of these terror inducing corporate buildings or perhaps both. You start to wonder why someone would 
build such a random store like this. You look around trying to find a reason, after a minute you spot it... 
Just to the East a little ways is what appears to be a Ranger Station, a Forest Safety Volunteer Center, 
and a massive Sign with a Fantasy Vibe that Says Lolishote forest.

<<keyOption [[Check Out Hard N' Ready|HNRLJS]]>>
<<keyOption [[Check out The Ranger Station|RSA]]>>
<<keyOption [[Check Out The Forest Safety Volunteer Center|FSVC]]>>
<<keyOption [[Enter Lolishote Forest|LSF]]>>
<<keyOption [[Go Back|centralPlaza]]>>

:: HNRLJS



:: RSA



:: FSVC



:: LSF




:: waterfrontDistrict

After a minute <<addMinutes 1>>of thought you decide it might be worthwhile checking out the town's "Beautiful 
and Enchanting" Waterfront you've heard so much about. You decide to head east into the Waterfront District, it 
takes 5 minutes <<addMinutes 5>> once you arrive it definitely lives up to it's name as you are greeted by a lush 
green waterfront, with beautiful bright blue water, and relaxing music playing over loudspeakers in various spots 
around the Waterfront District, it also has various benches and snack carts. You look around and notice a community 
school down the road to the east a little ways. Who knows maybe you could get a Job as a School Teacher Eventually. 
As you continue to scan the area you also see a building that could be a good way to find out if there are any Other 
Jobs in this area. CURRENTLY THERE ARE NO JOBS UNTIL CARRABINA IS READY TO IMPLEMENT MORE THANK YOU FOR YOUR PATIENCE.

<<keyOption [[Go Back|centralPlaza]]🔙>>

:: entertainmentDistrict

You are intrigued by the name Entertainment District. So you decide to head West. <<addMinutes 1>>
Once you reach The Entertainment District you are Greeted by 3 MASSIVE Gates made of Redwood and Silver.
The Gate On the left reads in huge Goofy Letters "KIDS ONLY." The Middle Gate reads in Beautiful Cursive Letters 
"Neutral Zone." And the gate on the right in Bright Neon Letters reads "Adults Only." You examine each gate
from a Distance and notice a barely visible Hole through the Bushes next to the KIDS ONLY Gate. Which proves that 
other Adults have probably snuck in before to "PLAY" with the kids or just get an eyeful of their cute little bodies.
You look around and notice just how many people are in the Entertainment District. Your Unsure if you'd be able to 
sneak a kid out of here without getting caught. But maybe you can find places within the District to "PLAY" with them
who knows... What to do what too do.

<<keyOption [[Sneak Into the Kids ONLY Sector|KOSEC]]>>
<<keyOption [[Enter The Neutral Zone|NEZ]]>>
<<keyOption [[Check Out The ADULTS ONLY SECTOR|AOSEC]]>>
<<keyOption [[Go Back|centralPlaza]]>>

:: KOSEC



:: NEZ



:: AOSEC



:: residentialDistrict

You head east into the residential District and are Immediately Bombarded with Half Naked Children running
around everywhere, Adults who are very closely watching their children, Restaurants, The Smell of Baked Goods 
Wafting through the air, and a CARE Job Office where you could probably apply for various Caregiver Jobs Such as
a Babysitter, a Nanny, or maybe even a Petsitter if you want. You look around and notice just how closely these
kids are being watched there's no way in hell you'll be able to sneak kids out of here.If you want some playtime 
with these gorgeous sunkissed Angels you may have to become a Babysitter, or Nanny.

<<keyOption [[Head into the CARE Building|CB]]>>
<<keyOption [[Go Back|centralPlaza]]>>

:: CB


